ORIGIN

This skill is original work by Seth J. Chandler. It encodes a method developed
and tested through mediation-competition packet review: reconstruct the case,
apply mandatory consistency and confidentiality gates, test mediation utility
and the settlement corridor, audit role-limited perspectives, forecast
clarifications, and score quality only after the gates pass.

The Lawve distribution package reorganizes the original reference materials
under resources/, adds portable document-capability fallbacks, catalogue
metadata, jurisdiction and confidentiality disclosures, and this licence and
notice. It does not alter the substantive validation gates or scoring rubric.

This skill is not affiliated with or endorsed by Lawve, any mediation
competition, or any dispute-resolution institution.

---

BUNDLED CODE

This package contains no executable code. It makes no network calls, spawns no
subprocesses, handles no credentials, and evaluates no dynamic code.

---

DISCLAIMER

This skill provides pedagogical quality control for fictional mediation
exercises. It does not provide legal advice, determine governing law, opine on
enforceability, or predict an actual dispute. Users remain responsible for
protecting confidential information, verifying jurisdiction-specific law,
checking source completeness, and keeping author-only findings separate from
participant-facing packets.
